Subject: [PATCH 04/15] Muscle Gap Analysis with one-tap Add to template (#8)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Closes the last outstanding roadmap item. Uses existing Training DNA
(weakest muscles) + the muscle-tagged 516-exercise library; no new
analytics, no schema change.

- domain/musclegap/MuscleGapAnalyzer.kt: for each weak muscle, suggests
  exercises that primarily train it, ranked compound/beginner-first and
  diversified by equipment (with a secondary-muscle fallback).
- TrainingDnaViewModel: computes muscleGaps from snapshot.weakestMuscles +
  library; adds addMuscleGapToTemplate() that creates a '<Muscle> Focus'
  template from the suggestions, plus a one-shot status message flow.
- Training DNA screen: 'Close the gaps' section under Weakest muscles —
  each weak muscle lists suggested exercises with a one-tap 'Add to
  template' button; transient confirmation banner.

Verified: full domain compiles on kotlinc 1.9.22 (167 classes); 4 logic
tests pass in-sandbox (suggestions, equipment diversification, blank/
missing filtering, secondary fallback). No tests committed.
